= Solution
{parent=i}

Multiply the two <power series> and collect equal powers of $x$. The <Cauchy product> gives
$$
\boxed{c_0=a_0b_0,\qquad c_1=a_0b_1+a_1b_0,\qquad c_2=a_0b_2+a_1b_1+a_2b_0.}
$$
Only terms whose two exponents add to the target exponent contribute.

= ii
{parent=b}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

In the <Cauchy product>, $a_jx^j$ combines with $b_{i-j}x^{i-j}$ to give a term of degree $i$. Hence
$$
\boxed{c_i=\sum_{j=0}^i a_jb_{i-j}.}
$$
This coefficient identity holds for <formal power series>. For convergent <Taylor series> it also gives the function product throughout the common open interval of convergence, where absolute convergence justifies regrouping.

